    "claude": {
      "SKILL.md": "---\nname: start\ndescription: Explicitly start or resume the GDSuperpowers guided game interview and lightweight build loop.\ndisable-model-invocation: true\n---\n\n# Start a game with GDSuperpowers\n\nThis is a thin entry alias, not a second game-design system. Locate and read the sibling `../gdsuperpowers/SKILL.md` relative to this installed skill directory. If unavailable, stop and report the missing companion; do not invent its instructions.\n\nTreat the user's remaining text as context for the main skill's `start` mode. With no text, begin or resume from existing project state. Read its interview guide before responding. Ask ONE unanswered game-direction question and wait. Do not dump a questionnaire or start building before a bounded design/plan approval. Preserve known genre, run-upgrade, persistence, and graphical preferences. An existing project resumes rather than resets.\n\nOnce discovery reaches an approved slice, continue through the main skill's normal build/verify/playtest loop. Never claim actual subagent or native BMAD execution without tool evidence.\n"
    },
    "codex": {
      "SKILL.md": "---\nname: start\ndescription: Explicitly start or resume the GDSuperpowers guided game interview and lightweight build loop.\n---\n\n# Start a game with GDSuperpowers\n\nThis is a thin entry alias, not a second game-design system. Locate and read the sibling `../gdsuperpowers/SKILL.md` relative to this installed skill directory. If unavailable, stop and report the missing companion; do not invent its instructions.\n\nTreat the user's remaining text as context for the main skill's `start` mode. With no text, begin or resume from existing project state. Read its interview guide before responding. Ask ONE unanswered game-direction question and wait. Do not dump a questionnaire or start building before a bounded design/plan approval. Preserve known genre, run-upgrade, persistence, and graphical preferences. An existing project resumes rather than resets.\n\nOnce discovery reaches an approved slice, continue through the main skill's normal build/verify/playtest loop. Never claim actual subagent or native BMAD execution without tool evidence.\n",
      "agents/openai.yaml": "interface:\n  display_name: \"Start Game\"\n  short_description: \"Guided game interview and Quick Flow Lite\"\n  default_prompt: \"Use $start to ask the next relevant game-direction question or resume my current GDSuperpowers game.\"\npolicy:\n  allow_implicit_invocation: false\n"
